From 1b5413de9a2c6b83f821c3d34368ac765234fd75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnTheFarm3r <104281500+JohnTheFarm3r@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:20:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: Autofocus statistics, sensor helpers and AF
 fixes

Compute the autofocus contrast the Af algorithm expects. In the centre
half of the window, every sampled block contributes the sum of two green
samples and the difference between the sums over two neighbouring runs
of blocks is squared. Averaging over blocks makes this a band pass that
follows image detail rather than pixel noise, which dominates single
pixel differences in low light. The result is normalised by the squared
mean so that exposure and gain changes do not look like focus changes.

Run the Af algorithm on fresh statistics only; it stepped the lens on
every frame with the values of the last statistics frame. Make the scan
steps, fine range, skipped statistics and the number of out of focus
statistics before a new scan tunable, compare
variances as floating point values, and move the lens also when a frame
start emitter is present.

Compute statistics on every second frame instead of every fourth, so that
the contrast scan takes half as long.

Add camera sensor helpers for the SmartSens SC820CS and SC1300CS.
